&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW235599363 BCX8&quot;&gt;The Senior Construction Project Manager is a career-level role with full ownership of an assigned construction scope of moderate to significant complexity within the Engineering, Procurement, &amp;amp; Construction (EPC) function. Working closely with the Construction Manager and Superintendents, this role coordinates with project management, infrastructure engineering, project controls, and procurement from preconstruction through completion and start of production. The role manages scheduling of trade contractors and vendor installations, resolves day-to-day construction issues, and tracks project schedule and budget, while owning RFIs, submittals, and procurement/RFPs for the assigned scope. The role &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW235599363 BCX8&quot;&gt;operates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW235599363 BCX8&quot;&gt; independently, applying sound judgment on schedule, cost, and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun ContextualSpellingAndGrammarErrorV2Themed SCXW235599363 BCX8&quot;&gt;risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW235599363 BCX8&quot;&gt; trade-offs, with work reviewed at key project milestones.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW235599363 BCX8&quot;&gt; This is an onsite role, with work performed in person.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
