&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The Senior Field Quality Engineer, Energy Storage is responsible for the quality, reliability, and safety of deployed battery energy storage system (BESS) assets, independently owning failure analysis and corrective action tracking for issues identified in the field. The role works closely with operations and maintenance teams, which perform routine monitoring and maintenance, and with service engineering, which owns advanced technical escalation, as well as with design, manufacturing, and supplier quality. The position identifies systemic quality issues, conducts structured investigations, drives corrective and preventive actions, and communicates fleet performance through statistical reporting and trend analysis. This is a fully on-site role at 100 Hooper in San Francisco, with semi-regular travel to field sites.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
