&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;page&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;layoutArea&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;column&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Redwood Materials&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Redwood Materials was founded in 2017 by JB Straubel, co-founder and former CTO of Tesla, on a simple but radical idea: the critical minerals powering the energy transition already exist. They just need to come back. Today Redwood is the largest lithium-ion battery recycler in North America — recovering, refining, and redeploying critical minerals from end-of-life batteries back into the supply chain. On the energy side, Redwood has deployed the largest second-life battery project in the world, delivering power to AI data centers in months rather than years using proprietary energy architecture engineered entirely in-house. The company is profitable, the market it operates in is projected to grow 20 to 50 times over the next decade, and Redwood is the only company with the supply chain, the technology, and the operational scale to lead it.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;&quot; data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Senior Finance Associate to join our Energy BD Finance group in San Francisco. In this role, you&#39;ll be part of the core team that owns the commercial finance function for our energy storage business — building and maintaining project finance models and supporting the end-to-end deal development, approval, and financing processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;&quot;&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;&quot; type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;&quot;&gt;Project Finance Modeling:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and maintain sophisticated project finance models for large-scale energy storage deployments, including scenario analysis, sensitivity testing, IRR/NPV outputs, and investor-ready presentations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;&quot;&gt;Deal Flow Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Business Development to support the full deal lifecycle — from initial screening and term sheet evaluation to contract negotiation — providing financial analysis and recommendations at each stage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;&quot;&gt;Deal Approvals:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the financial diligence and approval package for new energy storage transactions, structuring analysis that clearly frames risk, return, and strategic fit for executive and cross-functional review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;&quot;&gt;Pricing &amp;amp; Commercial Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop pricing frameworks that reflect true cost-to-serve and target returns, and partner with sales and BD to stress-test deal economics before commitment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;&quot;&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;&quot; type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;&quot;&gt;4–7 years of experience in renewables project finance with significant deal-facing responsibilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;&quot;&gt;Exceptional financial modeling skills — comfortable building complex, multi-scenario models from scratch in Excel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;&quot;&gt;Ability to structure ambiguous commercial situations into clear financial frameworks that drive decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;&quot;&gt;Strong communication and presentation skills, with experience distilling complex analyses for executive and investor audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;&quot;&gt;Self-starter mentality with high ownership and the ability to manage multiple live deal processes simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;&quot;&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;&quot; type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;&quot;&gt;Undergraduate or professional background in Electrical Engineering or a related technical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;&quot;&gt;Direct experience in energy storage, battery systems, or renewable energy project development and finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with tax equity structures, ITC qualification, and government incentive programs relevant to clean energy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ui-provider a b c d e f g h i j k l m n o p q r s t u v w x y z ab ac ae af ag ah ai aj ak&quot;&gt;In accordance with California pay transparency laws, the salary range for this position is listed below. Actual compensation may vary based on a variety of factors, including experience, education, and skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;California Pay Range:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$115,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$152,500 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;The position is full-time. Compensation will be commensurate with experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
