&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Redwood Materials is looking for a best-in-class Supplier Industrialization Engineer (SIE) to help scale our mechanical commodity suppliers across stampings, busbars, harnesses, CNC machined components, etc. to meet our aggressive production ramp schedules for our novel energy generation product. This is a fully on-site role at the San Francisco R&amp;amp;D Space, with 30% international travel to supplier sites. You will be responsible for ensuring all parts provided by your suppliers meet dimensional, functional, and reliability requirements. You will support ramping suppliers with detailed capacity analysis, process approvals, part qualifications, NPI builds, and ongoing supplier performance and audits. You are a doer, excited about getting your hands dirty and working in a dynamic, fast-paced setting with new technologies. The SIE will work closely with cross-functional partners in Supply Chain, Engineering, Finance, and Manufacturing to ensure that design and customer success targets are met.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support supplier audits (process, system, product) and risk assessments to help qualify new sources and ensure readiness for mass production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with GSMs, Design Engineering, and suppliers to align specifications, tolerance stack-ups, test coverage, and process controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review dimensional and quality reports, first article inspections, and other process control data to ensure part compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute PPAP/FAI activities and help define incoming inspection criteria based on part criticality, GD&amp;amp;T, and critical-to-quality key characteristics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support supplier non-conformance resolution, drive 8D investigations, and follow through with verification of effectiveness activities with vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain supplier scorecards with clear KPIs such as yield, PPM, delivery performance, and DFM responsiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support NPI builds and DFM/DFA feedback loops through early supplier engagement and pilot line walkthroughs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build and define a strong and capable network of vendor partners with robust process, technical capability, reliability, and capacity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support make-vs-buy, dual sourcing, and localization efforts across global supply chains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to sourcing decisions, lead-time analysis, and manufacturing footprint strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S. in Engineering, Supply Chain, Business, Economics or equivalent technical background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;M.S. in Industrial Engineering, Engineering Management, Supply Chain, and/or MBA a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of supplier quality, industrial engineering, process controls, or other related experience, ideally in automotive, industrial hardware, or other high-volume electronics manufacturing environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of mechanical fabrication processes: CNC machining, casting, injection molding, extrusion, sheet metal, riveting, welding, plating, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with PCBA manufacturing processes (SMT, through-hole wave and selective soldering, reflow oven profiles, test strategies, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency reading engineering drawings and applying GD&amp;amp;T; familiarity with dimension metrology (CMM, calipers, gauges) and statistical process control&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with APQP, PPAP, SPC, DFMEA/PFMEA, and ISO quality systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly collaborative, data-driven, and proactive; capable of thriving in fast-paced startup environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel internationally to supplier sites as needed (30%)&lt;/li&gt;
